# Visual Parity During Refactors

Architecture refactors should not change visual treatment by default.

## Rule

- Keep existing card/component visual treatment (layout, spacing, typography, interaction) unless the user asks for redesign.
- Separate structural refactors from visual updates when possible.
- If visual change is required, call it out explicitly and keep scope narrow.

## Verification

- Compare before/after for representative routes and breakpoints.
- Confirm empty states and reduced-motion behavior still match prior intent.
